    venue: ''
    focus: 'Re-dream #4 after: (1) Actual 4-model data now available — item_id=42.1%,
      model×item=33.6%, G_item=0.820, D-study prediction validated Δ=0.004; (2) Major
      framing revision per D006: recentered on model×item + IRT comparison as primary
      contributions, infrastructure→"precision separability" secondary, positioned
      as empirical extension of Mesting not new framework, removed unsupported "first"
      claims; (3) Two new robustness analyses: BF16-vs-FP16 shows precision→0.0006%
      without FP32, leave-one-model-out G_item spread=0.023; (4) 6 new bibliography
      entries addressing all-tier missing related work (Sclar''24, Kunievsky''25,
      Bui''25, binary G-theory literature); (5) Fine-tuning downgraded to Discussion
      observation; (6) Practitioner toolkit now concretely defined. Key question:
      do these changes push best≥7/10, median≥borderline accept, worst≥5/10?'
    what_if: []
